      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should immediately flush your eye with clean water for at least 15 minutes to dilute the chemical, then apply a few drops of sterile saline solution to soothe the irritation.\nAvoid using jojoba oil or lavender balm as they can trap the chemical against the eye and worsen the damage, so stick to plain water and saline only.\nIf the redness persists beyond an hour, you can take a single dose of over-the-counter acetaminophen for pain relief, but do not rub your eye.\nThis minor splash is a non-issue if you follow these steps, but if you see any vision changes, you must seek professional help immediately.",
      "source": "target",
